# Fractal Explorations in Secondary Mathematics, Science, and Computer Science.

**Authors:** Egnatoff, William J.

## Abstract
Fractal geometry is introduced through examples of computational exploration of coastlines, self-similar curves, random walks, and population growth. These explorations, which include the construction of algorithms and the subsequent development and application of simple computer programs, lend themselves to self-directed study and advanced student projects. (JJK)

